# Commit and push

When a task changes this repo, finish by committing and pushing. Do not wait to be asked.

Commit on the current branch and push to its upstream. On `main`, push to `origin/main`.

- Never update git config.
- Never force-push, hard-reset, or skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens). Leave those files out and say so.
- If the user says not to commit or not to push, stop there.
- One sentence, why rather than what, ending with a period. Pass the message with a HEREDOC.

Bump the version in the same commit when the change touches product code.
